course: dictionary
lesson: 1156
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Brim is a word with more than one meaning, and context tells you which one you need. Look at the words around it. «A hat with a wide brim shades your face, ears and neck.» Here a brim is the flat part of a hat that sticks out, so it is a noun.
explain: Brim can also mean the top edge of a cup, glass or bowl. If a glass is filled to the brim, it is full right up to its top edge. Try the swap test: put "top edge" in place of brim, and if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Brim can be a verb too, and it means to be full to the top. «Her eyes were brimming with tears» means her eyes were full of tears, not that they were moving. The word brimming often shows strong feeling, such as brimming with excitement.
fact: A brim is the top edge of a cup, glass or bowl, as in «full to the brim».
fact: A brim is also the flat part of a hat that sticks out and shades your face, ears and neck.
fact: To brim (with) means to be full to the top, as in «brimming with ideas».
fact: «Brimming» can show strong feeling, as in «eyes brimming with tears».
fact: «An ice cube floating in a glass filled to the brim does not make it overflow as it melts» because the melted water fills the space the ice was already taking up under the surface.
exercise: «A hat with a wide brim shades your face, ears and neck.» What is the brim of the hat? | The little badge at the front | The string that ties under your chin | *The flat part that sticks out and shades your face | The coloured band inside the top
exercise: «Her eyes were brimming with tears.» What does brimming mean here? | Running fast | Very cold | *Full to the top | Empty and dry
exercise: «The glass was filled to the brim.» Where is the brim? | In the middle, under the water | On the handle | *At the top edge of the glass | At the bottom of the glass
test: Jade says a brim is only part of a hat. What is the answer? | Yes, and only on caps | No, a brim is a kind of fish | *No, a brim can also be the top edge of a cup or glass | Yes, brims are only on hats
test: «An ice cube floating in a glass filled to the brim does not make it overflow as it melts.» What happens to the water as the ice melts? | The glass overflows and spills over the table | The glass empties completely | The ice grows bigger | *The water level stays about the same and does not overflow
exam: Which word means full to the top? | shallow | flat | *brimming | narrow
